114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 92 0 R
/T (The way people learn is changing fast because of digital learning platforms. These platforms generate a lot of data about how students interact with them. At first people tried to figure out which students might drop out by looking at things like their age, where they come from and their grades.. This did not give a complete picture of how students learn.Then came Learning Analytics and Educational Data Mining. These tools help us look at how students behave when they use learning platforms. We can see how often they log in if they do their assignments if they use the learning resources and if they engage with others online. All these things tell us a lot about how students learn and help us find out which students might be at risk of dropping out.)
/E (The way people learn is changing fast because of digital learning platforms. These platforms generate a lot of data about how students interact with them. At first people tried to figure out which students might drop out by looking at things like their age, where they come from and their grades.. This did not give a complete picture of how students learn.Then came Learning Analytics and Educational Data Mining. These tools help us look at how students behave when they use learning platforms. We can see how often they log in if they do their assignments if they use the learning resources and if they engage with others online. All these things tell us a lot about how students learn and help us find out which students might be at risk of dropping out.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 93 0 R
/T (Some studies have shown that looking at how students behave when they learn is better at predicting dropouts than looking at their age or grades. There are also datasets that help us compare how well different prediction models work.There is still a problem. Different studies use methods to prepare and analyze the data and they use different ways to evaluate the models. This means we do not always get the results.So researchers are looking for ways to predict dropouts using machine learning.)
/E (Some studies have shown that looking at how students behave when they learn is better at predicting dropouts than looking at their age or grades. There are also datasets that help us compare how well different prediction models work.There is still a problem. Different studies use methods to prepare and analyze the data and they use different ways to evaluate the models. This means we do not always get the results.So researchers are looking for ways to predict dropouts using machine learning.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
