>>
endobj
696 0 obj
<<
/Title (We also looked at the confusion matrix, which shows how many students the model correctly identified as being at risk or not at risk. The model correctly identified 3,841 students who were not at risk and 1,816 students who were at risk. It incorrectly identified 208 students who were at risk as not being at risk and 645 students who were not at risk as being at risk.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 698 0 R
/Next 694 0 R
>>
endobj
697 0 obj
<<
/Title (1. Logistic Regression: We used Logistic Regression as a model to classify students. It helps us figure out if a student is likely to drop out or stay in school based on things like who they're how they do in school and how they behave. Logistic Regression gives us the probability of a student dropping out or continuing.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 695 0 R
/Next 699 0 R
>>
endobj
698 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Tuned XGBoost model got an accuracy of 86.90%, a precision of 73.79%, a recall of 89.72%, an F1-score of 80.98% and a ROC-AUC of 94.58%. These results show that the model is good at identifying students who're at risk of dropping out and it does a good job overall.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 700 0 R
/Next 696 0 R
>>
endobj
699 0 obj
<<
/Title (2. Decision Tree: The Decision Tree model works by making rules based on things about the students. It is simple to understand. It helps us see what factors make a student more likely to drop out. Decision Tree looks at the features of the students. Makes decisions based on that.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 697 0 R
/Next 701 0 R
>>
endobj
700 0 obj
<<
/Title (To get an understanding of how well the Tuned XGBoost model works we looked at its performance in more detail. We already knew that it did well compared to the models but we wanted to see how it did on a more detailed level.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 702 0 R
/Next 698 0 R
>>
endobj
701 0 obj
<<
/Title (3. Random Forest: Random Forest is a way of combining Decision Trees to make better predictions. It does a job with complex data about students and their behavior. Random Forest helps us by reducing errors and making accurate predictions.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 699 0 R
/Next 703 0 R
>>
endobj
702 0 obj
<<
/Title (4.4 Performance Analysis of the Selected XGBoost Model)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 704 0 R
/Next 700 0 R
>>
endobj
703 0 obj
<<
/Title (4. XGBoost: XGBoost is a kind of algorithm that builds Decision Trees one after another to make better predictions. It is really good at finding the connections between how engaged a student's how well they do in school and if they are likely to drop out. XGBoost looks at the relationships between these things to make predictions.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 701 0 R
/Next 705 0 R
>>
endobj
